fallback applies \strong{unit by unit}: a unit whose N2 is \code{NA} takes its
T1 age when known. With FORMS-T, a unit the series does not cover takes
the proxy too.

Do not compare T2 values computed over different year windows. FORMS-T is
a height \strong{predicted} from Sentinel-1/2 and GEDI, not measured; light
thinnings (less than \code{seuil_perte}) are not seen.
